{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the elder said</b> Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 19:31) said: it is possible that he had another wife and she died first. But there is no need for this, for \"the elder\" (הַבְּכִירָה) is the opposite of \"the younger\" (צְעִירָה); any older one among brothers is called \"firstborn\" (בְּכוֹר), and any younger than him is \"younger\" (צָעִיר) to him, and the first fruit of the year is called \"first fruits\" (בִּכּוּרִים), and likewise \"the firstborn of the poor\" (בְּכוֹרֵי דַלִּים) (Isaiah 14:30) — those preceded in poverty, who are the poorest of the poor, and likewise \"with his firstborn he will found it and with his youngest he will set up its doors\" (בִּבְכֹרוֹ יְיַסְּדֶנָּה וּבִצְעִירוֹ יַצִּיב דְּלָתֶיהָ) (Joshua 6:26). And Onkelos likewise translates (Onkelos on Genesis 19:31): \"the elder one\" (רַבְּתָא)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:16.248263796Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}